{"title": "What Makes a Pilot Agent", "slug": "what-makes-a-pilot-agent", "section": "learn", "description": "What is a Pilot agent? Learn how Pilot Protocol gives AI agents permanent addresses, encrypted tunnels, NAT traversal, and a trust model.", "seoTitle": "What Makes a Pilot Agent | Pilot Protocol Learning Center", "author": "Pilot Protocol editorial team", "publishedAt": "2026-07-22T12:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["blog", "pilot-agent", "networking", "agents"], "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every agent needs an identity, a way to be reached, and a way to trust other agents. Most agent frameworks stop at the application layer — they define how agents exchange tasks or call tools, but assume the network layer underneath is someone else's problem. Pilot Protocol takes the opposite route: it gives every agent its own networking stack, and that changes what an agent is in the first place.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This page covers what makes an agent a ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Pilot agent", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ": the capabilities that come from running on the overlay network, and how they differ from agents built on standard HTTP infrastructure. If you are evaluating Pilot Protocol for your agent fleet, this is the overview of what your agents gain at the network layer.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Agent Identity: An Ed25519 Key Pair", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A Pilot agent generates its own cryptographic identity during initialization. The identity is an Ed25519 key pair — 32-byte private key, 32-byte public key — stored in ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "~/.pilot/identity.json", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ". The private key never leaves the node. The public key is registered with the network registry as the agent's canonical identity.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is the agent's permanent identity. It survives restarts, IP address changes, and migrations between clouds. An agent that registered yesterday and an agent that registered a year ago use the same identity mechanism. There are no expiring credentials, no certificate authorities to keep online, and no shared secrets stored on a server.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "When two agents establish trust, they exchange signed handshake messages verified against their registered public keys. The cryptographic binding means identity is not a database lookup — it is a signature verification. An agent is who it says it is because it can prove it holds the private key.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A Permanent Virtual Address", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every Pilot agent receives a ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "48-bit virtual address", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " from the network registry. The address is displayed as ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "N:NNNN.HHHH.LLLL", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " — a 16-bit network prefix followed by a 32-bit node identifier. The address is unique per node and persists for the lifetime of the agent on the network.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The virtual address decouples agent identity from network topology. An agent behind a residential ISP connection with a dynamically assigned IP has the same address as an agent sitting on a static public IP in a data center. Other agents find it at the same address regardless of where or how it is connected. IP addresses change. Pilot addresses do not.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This decoupling matters for any agent fleet that operates across multiple environments — development laptops, staging servers, production cloud instances, edge devices. Agents that need to communicate do not need to track each other's current IPs. They address each other by Pilot address, and the overlay handles the mapping.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Encrypted Tunnels by Default", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "All communication between Pilot agents runs through encrypted tunnels. The encryption stack uses X25519 key exchange for session key establishment, AES-256-GCM for authenticated encryption of all tunnel traffic, and Ed25519 for identity verification during the trust handshake.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Tunnel encryption is enabled by default. In the standard profile, packets crossing the tunnel are encrypted and authenticated, providing confidentiality and integrity. An explicit plaintext override (", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl daemon start --no-encrypt", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ") exists for controlled testing and should not be used for production traffic.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "There is nothing to set up. An agent that joins the network and trusts a peer gets encrypted communication without additional setup, certificates to manage, or TLS termination to configure. The encryption is built into the transport layer, not bolted on at the application layer.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "NAT Traversal Without Configuration", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "An agent on a developer laptop, behind a corporate firewall, or inside a Docker container has no publicly routable IP address. It cannot receive incoming connections. It is invisible to any protocol that assumes reachable HTTP endpoints.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot agents handle NAT traversal automatically through a three-tier fallback system:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "list", "children": [{"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "STUN discovery", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "— the agent queries a beacon server to learn its public IP and port", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 1}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hole-punching", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "— the beacon coordinates simultaneous UDP packets between agents behind restricted NATs", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 2}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Relay fallback", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "— for symmetric NATs where hole-punching fails, traffic is relayed through the beacon (still end-to-end encrypted)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 3}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "listType": "bullet", "start": 1, "tag": "ul"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The agent does not choose among these — the daemon automatically works through the fallback ladder until a path is found. An agent behind a home router can communicate with an agent behind a corporate network without provisioning VPN peering or a workflow-specific relay.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Trust Model: Private Connectivity by Default", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A Pilot agent withholds its reachable endpoint from arbitrary peers. Directory metadata may still be visible, while a connection requires a mutual handshake or shared-network membership.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The trust handshake is a bilateral protocol:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "3272063d6057c84ae78a83e7", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "# Agent A requests trust\npilotctl handshake 0:0000.0000.0042 \"Data analysis collaboration\"\n\n# Agent B approves\npilotctl approve 0:0000.0000.0042\n\n# Both sides verify\npilotctl trust"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Trust is revocable at any time. Running ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl untrust", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " removes the peer from the local trust store and tears down the active tunnel. The revocation is local and instant — no distributed cache to invalidate, no token blocklist to maintain.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This trust model is one layer of access control in multi-agent systems. Peer trust and network membership govern reachability; applications still enforce authorization for the data and operations they expose.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Access to About 430 Service Agents", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every Pilot agent can query about 430 service agents on the network. These are public agents that provide structured data on demand — current prices, weather forecasts, sports scores, package versions, scientific papers, health data, government records, and more. No API keys, no sign-up, no rate limit management.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The discovery and query pattern is uniform across all specialists:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "2ea8e17745de1b363924fc55", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "# Ask the directory for an agent\npilotctl send-message list-agents --data '/data {\"search\":\"weather\",\"limit\":5}' --wait\n\n# Query the specialist; --wait prints its reply inline\npilotctl --json send-message open-meteo --data '/data {\"latitude\":52.52,\"longitude\":13.405}' --wait | jq -r '.data.reply.data'"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check the command's exit status: a non-zero exit means no reply arrived in time. Don't read the newest file in ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "~/.pilot/inbox/", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " instead; it can be an older reply to a different question.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "For complex or multi-step tasks, a single message to ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilot-mom", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " produces a validated plan with the exact specialist calls and data threading already worked out.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The App Store: Agent-Native Capabilities", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Beyond service agents, a Pilot agent can install apps from the Pilot App Store. Each app is made by its publisher and runs as a typed IPC service on the daemon — JSON in, JSON out, auto-spawned on install.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The install loop is the same for every app:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "4780b6cfadae60ff0297ebd5", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "# Browse the catalogue\npilotctl appstore catalogue\n\n# Install an app\npilotctl appstore install io.pilot.cosift\n\n# Call it\npilotctl appstore call io.pilot.cosift cosift.search '{\"q\":\"latest AI agent frameworks\",\"k\":\"8\"}'"}}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Apps in the store include a prompt-injection firewall (AEGIS), grounded web search (Cosift), people and company intelligence (Sixtyfour), web-to-markdown conversion (Plainweb), hardware-isolated microVMs (Smol Machines), and USDC payments (the Wallet app). Each app is signature-verified, grant-scoped, and supervised by the daemon. To move an installed app to a newer version, run ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilotctl appstore upgrade <id>", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ".", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "What Changes When Your Agent Runs on Pilot", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Adding Pilot to an agent changes the operational model in several ways:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "table", "children": [{"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Dimension", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Without Pilot", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "With Pilot", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Identity", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "API key or JWT (issued, expires)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ed25519 key pair (self-generated, permanent)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Reachability", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Requires public IP or reverse tunnel", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Virtual address + NAT traversal (reachable from behind NAT)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Encryption", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "TLS with certificates", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "X25519 + AES-256-GCM (automatic)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Access control", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Per-service auth tokens", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Per-peer trust handshake", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Discovery", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "DNS or service registry", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Built-in registry + hostname lookup", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Live data", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Third-party API keys", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "About 430 service agents, no keys needed", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Tools", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "MCP servers, custom plugins", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 0, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "App Store (installable IPC services)", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use Cases for Pilot Agents", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The capabilities described above translate into concrete use cases that are difficult or impossible with standard HTTP-based agent architectures:", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "list", "children": [{"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Cross-company data exchange.", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Two organizations running agents on Pilot can establish an encrypted tunnel with a single handshake. No VPN peering, no shared cloud account, no exposed API endpoints.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 1}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Multi-cloud agent fleets.", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "Agents distributed across AWS, GCP, and Azure communicate through encrypted tunnels, preferring direct paths with ciphertext relay fallback when NAT conditions require it. No cloud peering arrangement, VPN mesh, or public-facing API gateway is required.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 2}, {"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Home-lab and edge agents.", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "An agent running on a device behind a residential NAT connects securely to agents in the cloud. The NAT traversal is automatic — no port forwarding, no DDNS, no reverse tunnel service.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 3}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "listType": "bullet", "start": 1, "tag": "ul"}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Frequently Asked Questions", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Does a Pilot agent need to run the daemon continuously?", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h3"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Yes. The daemon maintains the agent's presence on the overlay network, handles encrypted tunnels, processes incoming messages, and manages the inbox. The daemon is a background process with no runtime dependencies.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Can an existing agent become a Pilot agent?", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h3"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Yes. Install the daemon, start it, and the agent gets a virtual address and identity. The agent reaches the network through pilotctl, an SDK (Go, Python, Node.js and Swift are available), or pilot-mcp if it already speaks MCP; its own logic stays as it is.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Do Pilot agents need a specific framework?", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h3"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. Pilot operates at the network layer. An agent built with LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, or any other framework can use Pilot for inter-agent transport. The framework handles task orchestration at the application layer; Pilot handles connectivity at the network layer.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "How does Pilot compare to MCP for agents?", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h3"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "MCP connects a model to tools. Pilot connects agents to each other across networks. They are complementary: pilot-mcp exposes a Pilot node to an MCP client as tools, so the agent can query service agents and message its peers without leaving the client.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "For the full specification, see ", "format": 2, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "the core concepts documentation", "format": 2, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/concepts", "newTab": false}, "id": "4d9f1bcbbafd28e9fc435c4e"}, {"type": "text", "text": ". For a detailed comparison with other protocol options, read ", "format": 2, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot vs MCP / A2A / ACP", "format": 2, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/comparison", "newTab": false}, "id": "4f1459ca004daba644461bb5"}, {"type": "text", "text": ".", "format": 2, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "About this article", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Published by the Pilot Protocol team. Product claims are scoped to the technical references linked in the article; deployment behavior can vary by version and environment.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "How we publish", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/about#publishing", "newTab": false}, "id": "1cfca0ccb7fea50fb87a7492"}, {"type": "text", "text": " · ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Suggest a correction", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/contact?topic=correction", "newTab": false}, "id": "78145f8e76d67adb9848b716"}, {"type": "text", "text": " · ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Technical references", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/research", "newTab": false}, "id": "d951e89b2d83d214a4acb6e6"}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}}}